{"name":"Smallmouth Bass","hex":"#ac9a7e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"smallmouth bass","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of smallmouth (fish)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smallmouth_bass"}],"entries":[{"title":"Smallmouth bass","blocks":[{"text":"The smallmouth bass is a species of freshwater fish in the sunfish family (Centrarchidae) of the order Centrarchiformes. It is the type species of its genus Micropterus, and is a popular game fish sought by anglers throughout the temperate zones of North America, and has been spread by stocking —as well as illegal introductions—to many cool-water tributaries and lakes in Canada and more so introduced in the United States. The maximum recorded size is approximately 27 inches (69 cm) and 12 pounds (5.4 kg)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Smallmouth_Bass_%2849561724026%29.jpg/330px-Smallmouth_Bass_%2849561724026%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smallmouth_bass"},{"title":"Bass (fish)","blocks":[{"text":"Bass is a common name shared by many species of ray-finned fish from the large clade Percomorpha, mainly belonging to the orders Perciformes and Moroniformes, encompassing both freshwater and marine species. The word bass comes from Middle English bars, meaning \"perch\", despite that none of the commonly referred bass species belong to the perch family Percidae."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bass_(fish)"},{"title":"Ferry Bridge, Dorset","blocks":[{"text":"Ferry Bridge is at the beginning of the causeway to the Isle of Portland, Dorset, England, and is the point at which the Fleet lagoon joins Portland Harbour. It is situated several hundred metres south of Portland's boundary with the village of Wyke Regis, Weymouth. To the west of Ferry Bridge is the start of The Fleet, which is an internationally important nature reserve that extends to Abbotsbury Swannery, while to the east is Portland Harbour. Along the harbour side is Smallmouth Beach. The only road between Portland and the Mainland passes across Ferry Bridge."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Ferrybridge_-_geograph.org.uk_-_161528.jpg/330px-Ferrybridge_-_geograph.org.uk_-_161528.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferry_Bridge%2C_Dorset"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Smallmouth_bass.png/500px-Smallmouth_bass.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Smallmouth_bass.png/500px-Smallmouth_bass.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASmallmouth_bass.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Smallmouth_Bass_%28Micropterus_dolomieu%29.jpg/500px-Smallmouth_Bass_%28Micropterus_dolomieu%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Smallmouth_Bass_%28Micropterus_dolomieu%29.jpg/960px-Smallmouth_Bass_%28Micropterus_dolomieu%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Smallmouth_Bass_%28Micropterus_dolomieu%29.jpg/500px-Smallmouth_Bass_%28Micropterus_dolomieu%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASmallmouth_Bass_(Micropterus_dolomieu).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Detailed_underwater_photo_of_smallmouth_bass_fish_micropterus_dolomieu.jpg/330px-Detailed_underwater_photo_of_smallmouth_bass_fish_micropterus_dolomieu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_c